{
  // A relative path rather than the package name `@cue/config/tsconfig/node.json`.
  // That form resolves through node_modules, which works for every tool that
  // fully replicates npm's resolution — but `@cue/config` is a devDependency,
  // and Vercel's Node.js function builder traces and prunes the dependency
  // tree for the deployed function separately from the project's own install,
  // legitimately excluding devDependencies as build-time-only. When that pass
  // couldn't resolve the extends target, it silently fell back to bare
  // compiler defaults instead of failing loudly — which surfaced as an
  // unrelated-looking type error deep in application code rather than a
  // missing-config error. A relative path resolves by plain filesystem lookup
  // and needs no package resolution at all, so it can't be affected by
  // dependency pruning in any build environment.
  //
  // The relative form then hit the *opposite* failure. A filesystem lookup
  // needs the file to actually be on disk, and a build whose context is this
  // directory alone has no `../../packages/` to find — workspace *imports*
  // still resolved, because the root install symlinks them into node_modules,
  // but `extends` is not an import. TypeScript again fell back to bare
  // defaults in silence, and bare defaults mean `strict: false`, which turns
  // off narrowing of discriminated unions: ten TS2339s appeared in code that
  // was correct, on a union whose `if (!x.allowed)` branch no longer narrowed.
  //
  // So neither form is dependable on its own. The strictness this repo relies
  // on is therefore restated below rather than only inherited. It is a floor,
  // not a replacement for the shared config: when the extends resolves these
  // are redundant, and when it does not they are the only thing standing
  // between a silent downgrade and a build that type-checks what it claims to.
  // `.github/workflows/ci.yml` asserts the effective config still has them.
  "extends": "../../packages/config/tsconfig/node.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "build.js"]
}
